  exactMappings:
  - 'startSize  <- minSize/maxSize: 3..5'
  - 'startLifetime <- minEnergy/maxEnergy: 3..6'
  - startRotation <- rndRotation=False (0..360deg random when true)
  - simulationSpace <- 'Simulate in Worldspace?'=False
  - scalingMode=Shape (legacy did not scale particle size with transform scale)
  - playOnAwake <- m_Emit=True
  - velocityOverLifetime space = Local
  - 'localVelocity contribution: (0, 0, 0)'
  - 'worldVelocity contribution: (0, 0, 0)'
  - 'rndVelocity: (0, 0, 0) (as +/- envelope)'
  - shape -> Sphere radius 0.12 scale (1, 1, 1)
  - colorAnimation 5 keys -> ColorOverLifetime gradient (keys at 0/25/50/75/100%)
  - 'damping=1: documented legacy semantics is NO damping (velocity held constant
    until the particle dies). VOLT left constant - exact.'
  - renderMode Billboard
  - 'renderer copy: material/shadows/probes/sorting/cameraVelocityScale/lengthScale/velocityScale/maxParticleSize'
  - 'NOTE: ''exact'' classifications are static-analysis only - every mapping still
    requires visual verification in-engine.'
  approximations:
  - 'emission rate: legacy re-rolls min..max per emission event; Shuriken min/max
    rate sampling interval differs - verify perceived grain at low rates (1..4/s)'
  - legacy adds the velocity contributions at SPAWN; Shuriken VelocityOverLifetime
    applies them over the whole particle life. For constant-velocity contributions
    this phase coincides; combined with the damping curve this should reproduce legacy
    motion - VERIFY per emitter.
  - 'tangentVelocity=(0.12, 0.12, 0.12): legacy computes a per-particle tangent to
    the ellipsoid surface at the spawn point (a swirl). Shuriken 2017.4 has no tangential
    mode; V2 uses +/- per-axis VelocityOverLifetime envelope. Trajectory distribution
    differs - VERIFY (worst on ''Cloud''/''Cloud_bad'' systems).'
  - 'velocity rotation experiment attached - OPTIONAL, OFF (enableVelocityRotation=false)
    until enabled in the Inspector. Reproduces the STAGE 5 MEASURED legacy velocity
    rotation dv/dt = localRotationAxis x velocity with the UNNORMALIZED axis (Cloud_bad:
    (0.2,0.2,0.2), rate omega = |a|*sin(angle(v0,ahat)) <= |a| = 0.3464 rad/s = 19.85
    deg/s; |v| conserved; per-step fit error 1.35e-4 vs 0.033 for the reversed sign).
    Implementation approximations: (1) per-frame Quaternion.AngleAxis(|a|*dt, ahat)
    rotation in LOCAL sim space - exact rotation of the velocity vector, whereas legacy
    integrates pos += v*dt per step with the same law (measured advvection residual
    1.2e-4/step); (2) while ON the VOLT module is DISABLED so the per-frame velocity
    writes are the only velocity influence (doc investigation: VOLT adds its own per-frame
    velocity on top of the carried Particle.velocity; composition order undocumented)
    - engine-side double-apply behavior still to be validated in the in-engine A/B;
    (3) fresh spawns identified by Particle.randomSeed get ONE uniform sample of the
    captured VOLT constant-family baselines, so the initial-velocity DISTRIBUTION
    is unchanged (no new spawn-velocity model this stage, per Stage 5: all candidate
    spawn-direction laws were rejected; measured fresh structure is 100% outward radial
    0.189 +/- 0.043 plus random-direction tangential 0.133 +/- 0.074, |v0| = 0.239
    +/- 0.056); (4) fresh spawns are first seen in the LateUpdate after their birth
    sim step, so movement starts one frame after emission (~|v0|/frameRate local units);
    (5) particles alive at takeover start rotating mid-flight WITHOUT velocity rewrites;
    (6) restored behavior is exact for new spawns; particles alive across a restore
    keep their rotated velocities until they die (VOLT resumes contributing on top
    when re-enabled); (7) if a Stage-3b velocity multiplier is attached, spawn velocities
    come from the rotation component''s OWN first-capture baseline, so multiplier
    edits do not affect spawn velocities mid-experiment; (8) do NOT enable simultaneously
    with the Stage-2 orbit or Stage-4 tangent emitter (runtime warns; one knob at
    a time). NOT validated in-engine yet.'
  unsupported:
  - emitterVelocityScale=0.12 is documented as inert unless 'Simulate in Worldspace?'
    is enabled; this system simulates local, so legacy applies no emitter-velocity
    inheritance - nothing converted (V1 mapped it unconditionally and wrongly).
  - 'rotation axes localRotationAxis=(0.2, 0.2, 0.2) worldRotationAxis=(0, 0, 0):
    orbital position rotation is NOT representable by any 2017.4 Shuriken module (orbital
    velocity ships only in 2019.1+). Nothing was encoded by the module conversion
    - VERIFY after Stage-1 testing by using ''Attach Orbit Script (selection)'' on
    this holder (speed unit undocumented; calibrate with the Inspector multiplier).'
  warnings:
  - Legacy components were preserved (not modified, not disabled, not deleted). Delete
    the [PSV2] child to revert.
  - Runtime code that searches GetComponentsInChildren<ParticleSystem> under this
    hierarchy will now also see the converted system.
  - Runtime scripts that disable legacy ParticleRenderer (e.g. Arrow.cs) will NOT
    hide the converted system until the cutover stage.
  - 'NOTE: legacy runtime toggling of m_Emit after startup has no automatic Shuriken
    equivalent; verify no script relies on it for [PSV2] Cloud_bad'
  - 'holder local/world scale is not (1,1,1): converted value ranges were computed
    from world/local directions and should be re-verified after any parent scale change.'
